---
description: Use when asked for architecture docs, a TDD, ADRs, design docs, an exec brief or roadmap for a data platform, or when editing files under docs/architecture/.
globs: docs/architecture/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Use the `architecture-docs` skill to orchestrate this work, and its focused
skills for each part (`project-facts`, `architecture-decision`, `engineer-pack`,
`director-pack`, `executive-pack`, `data-contracts`, `validate-architecture-docs`,
`review-architecture-docs`).

- Ground first: the facts file `ground:` block (decision, outcome, terrain,
  falsifiers, owner, single action in one sentence) comes before any doc.
- `docs/architecture/00-project-facts.yaml` is the single source of truth. Change
  a fact there first, then every doc that uses it.
- Same facts across the executive, director and engineer packs. Different altitude only.
- Mark unknowns as `ASSUMPTION [A-###]` or `OPEN QUESTION [Q-###]`.
- Mermaid for diagrams. No em dashes.
- After edits, run `validate-architecture-docs`.
